message: >
  If you use this software or the accompanying preprint in your research,
  please cite the Zenodo preprint below. Commercial use requires a separate
  license (see COMMERCIAL.md).
type: software
title: >
  KDF: A Deterministic Architecture for Finite-Resource Information
  Preservation—Cross-Domain Evidence and Self-Refutation of Canonical Values
abstract: >
  KDF (Knowledge Decay Framework) is a deterministic graph-compression
  technique for finite-resource information preservation. Selected nodes are
  preserved verbatim while unselected nodes are discarded, distinguishing KDF
  from content-transforming methods such as LLM-based fact extraction.
  Cross-domain evidence from 67 verified findings; includes transparent
  self-refutation of the patent's canonical values across four benchmarks.
